== Reconciliation boundary

The current colour-product owner recognizes adjoint chains on summed cycles and
materializes only those chains with its reserved dummy state. It publishes only
a successful existing two-f or shortest-cycle contraction. Opening alone never
becomes a rewrite, so collection cannot oscillate with expansion. Summed edges
exclude fixed components; chain endpoint dimensions and every generator must
match. Spectator factors remain products. This is a colour identity, not graph
numerator distribution. Authoritative tensor interfaces and dummy history remain
with their existing owners.

The source applies to current colour APIs without source44 or source45 code.
This parallel preparation does not complete source46 in the sequential main
replay: integration after source45 needs fresh combined checks and review on the
actual combined head. The approved MAIN39--43 base retains the later Idenso
architecture, documentation registry, local Kurbo and root-host selection
owners; this refresh changes none of them beyond registering this note.
No fundamental, Dirac, inference or planner redesign is included.

